i think it's fun to be a little playful  and do something people won't normally  do with something like a donut hi i'm  alexander and i'm going to show you how  to make some of my signature animal  donuts  so you'll start with your dry  ingredients your flour sugar salt baking  powder baking soda you'll whisk those  all together with your hands you can  just break in the butter until it's  practically invisible until you can no  longer see large chunks a few years ago  i found myself living in paris i didn't  speak very good french so i was having a  hard time finding a baking job much to  my chagrin if you feel chagrin it means  you are embarrassed or distressed as a  result of failure  i decided i would try to do my own  project so i started a crowdfunding  campaign for what i wanted to be a donut  cart so basically i had a tricycle with  a huge box on it and a chalkboard and i  would write my flavors on there and just  pull up in the street illegally and sell  my donuts on the weekends since i was  doing a crowdfunding campaign i wanted  to make something that would maybe be  like instagramable or you know get me  noticed apart from other crowdfunding  campaigns and i'm also in love with cats  so i thought why don't i combine like  two of my favorite things and make a cat  doughnut so i tried a few different ways  and i settled on a really simple design  since the cat donuts were so popular i  decided to try a few other animals like  a bear and a dog and frogs if you aspire  to be a baker or a pastry chef one thing  you should know is that it's all about  repetition so you'll do the same thing  hundreds and hundreds of times but  there's some beauty in that  for the cat i'll just cut away a tiny  chunk a small triangle at the top of the  donut to make ears for the dog i'll use  the same cutter i use for the middle of  the donut and just cut away a little  cheek to make like a snout and some  droopy ears for the bear and the frog  they're actually the same design but  we're going to decorate them differently  and we're just going to use donut holes  as the ears so we don't have to waste  anything you can just attach them with a  bit of water or egg white or milk when  you're frying the donuts it's going to  be about a minute on each side and you  don't want to flip it more than once or  it's going to get oily when they're  ready they'll have a very prominent  golden brown color so i'm going to make  just a classic vanilla glaze with some  powdered sugar honey and milk make sure  you sift your powdered sugar for the  glaze or it'll end up clumpy you can  flavor it with anything like fruit juice  and you can color it any color you want  it to be when i began baking  several years ago i always thought like  a donut was super hard to make and it  was like the mark of a good baker which  is not necessarily true it is scary to  fry them but they're pretty easy to make  especially cake doughnuts you don't even  need a mixer the first time i made  donuts i actually forgot sugar so when i  went to fry them they were basically  biscuits oops  i think i became obsessed with donuts  when i was younger me and my family  would go get donuts at this place on the  boardwalk every summer they were like 50  cents each they would melt in your mouth  you'd get them in a bag all melted  together and they were amazing so i'm  just gonna judge these up with a little  bit of melted chocolate and give them  some cute faces i'll draw some little  ears on the cats and their eyes and  whiskers the dogs will get some bigger  ears and some little freckles on their  snout  the bears will fill in their ears just  little circles and give them a little  smiley face and then the frogs will use  a little more white glaze to make like  an eyeball and then we'll wait for that  to dry before we put a little more  chocolate on there we're gonna do a  smiley with the chocolate also and with  some of the leftover pink glaze i'm just  gonna pipe some small tongs on them my  favorite part about making donuts is  giving them to people and seeing the  look of joy on their face  i hope you'll love these adorable donuts  as much as i do you really don't have to  be a professional baker to make  something great to share with your  family and friends  [Music]  so good  oh yes  you
 

